  "body": "## What\n\nArchive the historical coordinator prompt and generated state that started session `26834c4f-a585-4314-bb86-c1f6141aa9ee`. Replace the superseded draft handoff page with links to both dated archive pages. Merge current `main` into the branch.\n\n## Why\n\nThe incoming session started from the local `.holding/handoff/2026-09-26-a8fde4b6.md` and adjacent generated state, rather than the draft in this PR. The coordinator's 2026-09-26 note directs this PR to preserve those actual inputs.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Harness: Codex CLI 0.157.1. Model: `gpt-6-sol` at medium effort.\n- `reports/inputs/handoff-114-archive-evidence.md` records source hashes, byte comparisons, the redacted secret scan, no redactions, review reproduction, and local checks.\n- `mise run check`, `mise run check:mutation`, `mise run build`, and `mise run docs:build` passed locally. The normal commit hooks, including staged gitleaks, passed.\n- `mise run docs:check-links` could not validate unchanged Mermaid pages because sandboxed Chromium was denied. Five links in unchanged pages were reported invalid; no archive link was reported invalid. CI's `docs` job is the site and link gate.\n\n## Docs\n\n`docs/src/content/docs/project/handoff.md` now points to the prompt and state archives. The source text is preserved verbatim after frontmatter and a short provenance note. The tooling page records the narrow prose exemptions.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] All required CI checks concluded success\n- [x] Docs updated\n- [x] No secrets in committed changes\n- [x] Evidence committed\n\nRefs: #114\n",
